eleration. 2. Tensile stress and longitudinal strain induced in the 12 mm steel cable during acceleration. 3. Drum mass moment of inertia, angular acceleration, and driving torque. 4. Elevator kinetic energy, drum rotational kinetic energy, and total kinetic energy at 3.6 m/s. 5. Mechanical power delivered at the drum and minimum motor power at 3.6 m/s. 6. Total work done by the motor to raise the elevator 15 m (accounting for both acceleration and constant speed phases). 7. Total travel time and average motor power required over the entire 15 m lift. Clearly state all equations, intermediate values, units, and final outputs."}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_force', 'description': "Calculate force using Newton's second law.\n\nFormula:\n    F = m * a\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Force in Newtons (N).", 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_mass', 'description': 'Calculate mass from force and acceleration.\n\nFormula:\n    m = F / a\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Mass in kilograms (kg).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_acceleration', 'description': 'Calculate acceleration from force and mass.\n\nFormula:\n    a = F / m\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n\nReturns:\n    Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'mass': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'mass'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_torque', 'description': 'Calculate torque.\n\nFormula:\n    τ = r * F * sin(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    lever_arm: Distance from pivot in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and lever arm in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Torque in Newton-meters (N·m).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'lever_arm': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 90.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'lever_arm'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_work', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical work.\n\nFormula:\n    W = F * d * cos(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    displacement: Displacement in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and displacement in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Work in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'displacement': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 0.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'displacement'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_energy', 'description': 'Calculate kinetic energy.\n\nFormula:\n    KE = 1/2 * m * v²\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    velocity: Velocity in meters per second (m/s).\n\nReturns:\n    Kinetic energy in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'velocity': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'velocity'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_power', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical power.\n\nFormula:\n    P = W / t\n\nArgs:\n    work: Work in Joules (J).\n    time: Time in seconds (s).\n\nReturns:\n    Power in Watts (W).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'work': {'type': 'number'}, 'time': {'type': 'number'}}, 'requ