f 2.57e4 or 25700).\n3. Always return exact raw floating-point calculations in the calculation_result dictionary.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "An 800 kg elevator is suspended by a solid steel cable (12 mm diameter, Young's Modulus E = 200 GPa) wrapped around a winch drum. The drum has a mass of 150 kg, a radius of 0.20 m, and a radius of gyration of 0.15 m. The elevator accelerates upward from rest at 1.8 m/s² until reaching a maximum velocity of 3.6 m/s, after which it continues at constant velocity for a total lifting distance of 15 m. The motor drives the drum through a gearbox with 90% efficiency. Determine: 1. Net accelerating force and required cable tension during acceleration. 2. Tensile stress and longitudinal strain induced in the 12 mm steel cable during acceleration. 3. Drum mass moment of inertia, angular acceleration, and driving torque. 4. Elevator kinetic energy, drum rotational kinetic energy, and total kinetic energy at 3.6 m/s. 5. Mechanical power delivered at the drum and minimum motor power at 3.6 m/s. 6. Total work done by the motor to raise the elevator 15 m (accounting for both acceleration and constant speed phases). 7. Total travel time and average motor power required over the entire 15 m lift. Clearly state all equations, intermediate values, units, and final outputs."}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': None, 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'fc_c1fc36e6-9bf4-48eb-bbce-2342f2a626e2', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_stress', 'arguments': '{"area": 0.00011309733552923255, "force": 9288}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'content': '82123950.635418', 'tool_call_id': 'fc_c1fc36e6-9bf4-48eb-bbce-2342f2a626e2'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'response_format': {'type': 'json_object'}, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7}}
